<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-SKAARDAL WINS MEN'S SUPER-G GOLD.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SKAARDAL WINS MEN'S SUPER-G GOLD.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defending champion Atle Skaardal of Norway won the men's super-giant slalom gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Monday in a provisional time of one minute 29.68 seconds.  </p>
<p>Norway's Lasse Kjus was second in 1:29.89 and Guenther Mader of Austria third in 1:30.01.</p>
